Single-library natives (darwin-arm64, darwin-x64, linux-x64):
libjpdfium is one shared library that statically links all of the above
plus the code PDFium bundles (Skia, Abseil, PartitionAlloc, FreeType,
HarfBuzz, ICU with trimmed ICU data, libpng, zlib, Brotli, OpenJPEG,
Little CMS, libjpeg-turbo) and libjpeg-turbo/TurboJPEG (with libspng and
zlib) for QPDF and the bridge. Every component is under a permissive licence
whose notice travels in the natives jar's licenses/ directory; static
linking adds no further obligation. Chromium's libc++, linked where a
platform's PDFium build uses it, is Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception, which
waives attribution for compiled object code. libjpeg-turbo: this software is
based in part on the work of the Independent JPEG Group.

